ReadyStack 0004: virt-handler's image defaults to a non-root user (qemu, uid 107).

ReadyStack images never default to root (owner 2026-10-28). virt-handler still runs as root: the KubeVirt CR in the
install bundle sets runAsUser: 0 on its container (spec.customizeComponents). One line in cmd/virt-handler/BUILD.bazel.

--- a/cmd/virt-handler/BUILD.bazel
+++ b/cmd/virt-handler/BUILD.bazel
@@ -201,5 +201,8 @@
     tars = [
         "virt-handler-tar",
     ],
+    # ReadyStack: non-root default user (qemu, uid 107). virt-handler gets root from its pod: runAsUser 0 is set
+    # through the KubeVirt CR spec.customizeComponents patch shipped in the install bundle.
+    user = "107",
     visibility = ["//visibility:public"],
 )
